        DocBook Abstract
XML
<abstract>
<para>Setting up a systemd service on &productname; allows administrators to automate process execution, manage application lifecycles, and configure custom background tasks. By defining declarative unit files, users can specify service dependencies, control startup behavior, and apply security sandboxing features. This ensures reliable background operation, simplifies troubleshooting with systemctl, and improves overall system stability across system reboots.</para>
<para><emphasis>Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Basic understanding of Linux commands</para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Basic understanding of Linux processes, daemons, and control groups</para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
